A file contains these three lines. On which line number does tsc report an error?

let n: number = 5;
n = n + 1;
n = "five";

tsc compiles this file. What does the JavaScript file contain?

export const x: number = 1;
export interface A { a: number }

The compiled program from the figure runs. What does it print?

interface User { name: string }
const u: User = JSON.parse('{"id": 7}');
console.log(u.name);

let n: number = 5;
n = "five";
Which message does the compiler report on the second line?

function area(r) { return r * r; }
const n = 5;
let s = "a";
function twice(x: number) { return x + x; }
const ok = true;
How many of these five declarations are missing an annotation that the compiler needs?

const day = "mon";
let d2 = day;
What type does TypeScript infer for d2?

interface Named { name: string }
class Dog { name = "d"; bark() {} }
const n: Named = new Dog();
Does this compile? Answer yes or no.

interface Named { name: string }
The values below are each held in a variable and then assigned to a variable of type Named.
1: { name: "a" }
2: { name: "a", age: 3 }
3: { id: 7 }
4: { name: 5 }
5: an instance of a class with name = "d" and a method bark()
How many of the five fit Named?

interface P { readonly x: number; y: number }
const p: P = { x: 1, y: 1 };
p.x = 2;
p.y = 2;
p.x = p.x + 1;
On how many lines does the compiler report an error?

interface Named { name: string }
class Cat { label = "c"; lives = 9 }
const n: Named = new Cat();
What does the compiler do?

interface P { readonly id: number; name: string }
const p: P = { id: 1, name: "a" };
p.name = "b";
p.id = 2;
p.id = p.id;
How many lines report an error?

function f(x: string | number) {
  x.toString();
  x.valueOf();
  x.toUpperCase();
}
How many of the three lines compile without an error?

function f(x: string | number | boolean) {
  if (typeof x === "string") return 1;
  if (typeof x === "number") return 2;
  return x;
}
How many types may x have on the last line?

type Shape = circle | rect | tri | line
A switch handles circle, rect and tri, and its default branch contains const _x: never = s;
The error says the type with kind "___" is not assignable to never. Which kind fills the gap?

function f(x: string | number | null) {
  if (x === null) return 0;
  if (typeof x === "string") return 1;
  return ???;
}
Which expression is allowed at ???

type U = "a" | "b" | "c";
A switch on a value u of type U handles only case "a", and its default branch contains const x: never = u;
The error says the leftover type is not assignable to never. How many members does the leftover union have?

